// EXPECT: E0214 — no implicit conversion between an integer and a float (ADR-0040 §6)
// `cast` is the only way across, exactly as it is between integer widths. This is stricter
// than C, and it is the strictness ADR-0016's typing rules already have: adding one
// implicit conversion for floats would make the float the only type that silently changes
// another's meaning.
main :: () {
    n: s64 = 1;
    f: float64 = 1.5;
    bad := n + f;
}
